    "result_text": "Both findings were valid, and I addressed them.\n\n## Changes\n\nI agreed with both findings \u2014 they correctly identify that the inline formula duplicated domain logic that this codebase deliberately centralizes.\n\n1. **New `MembershipNumber` model helper** (`model/MembershipNumber.java`) \u2014 a `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` static derivation in the exact style of the sibling `MembershipLevel` and `OwnerIdentity` classes, documented as the single source of truth for the `<customerCode>-M<YY>` format.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java:24`** now calls `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` instead of inlining the formula.\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** calls `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` alongside `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`, so the two derived values are handled consistently and the private helper is gone \u2014 the class is purely an emitter again.\n\nNow the formula lives in one place; if the spec at `openapi.yml:2121` changes, only `MembershipNumber` needs updating. `BusinessDay`'s reference to \"the membership number's year segment\" now points at a named home for the concept.\n\nTests: full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 test, 0 failures), so acceptance behaviour is intact.",
